  "configuration_id": "config_009",
  "reason": "Evidence: Multiprofile + scvi_n200 is clearly the strongest direction (0.650-0.653 vs ~0.52 singleprofile), and transformer ≈ avgpool (0.3% gap, likely noise). The image modality is very weak (resnet50: 0.21), so multimodal gains are uncertain. Key uncertainty: whether the RNA encoder choice still matters within the multiprofile setting, and whether an alternative encoder (scgpt) can push past 0.65. Question tested: config_009 changes only the RNA encoder from scvi_n200 to scgpt while holding multiprofile + transformer fixed, isolating the encoder effect in the best-performing structural context. Why this is best: it is a single-variable extension of the current best (config_006), directly exploitative of the strongest signal, and simultaneously tells us whether scgpt is competitive or inferior—information that would guide all future encoder choices. If scgpt matches or beats scvi_n200, we gain a new best; if it lags, we confirm scvi_n200 is well-suited and can focus budget on other axes (e.g., multimodal fusion or image encoder quality)."
}

